WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:06.400
Speaker 1: Also interesting yesterday, CNN
was able to get an interview with President

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.360
Zelensky in his bunker.

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:15.019
He's been in a bunker for some period of time
and occasionally exiting the bunker to record

00:00:15.019 --> 00:00:17.560
videos and do different things that we have
seen.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:22.430
CNN's Matthew Chance spoke with Zelensky in
the bunker about what's going on with negotiations

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:24.890
and other things, and it is incredible to
see

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:30.330
Speaker 3: you send your delegation to meet
the Russians for talks.

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:33.480
Did anything substantial come out of that?

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:37.180
Is there any hope as the world watches for
diplomacy?

00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:46.760
They decided they decided to begin to speak
about the situation and I wanted I really

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:48.870
wanted and I told them.

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:49.870
You have to speak.

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:59.440
First of all, you everybody has to stop, stop
fighting and to go to that points from where

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:00.850
it is was beginning.

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:04.839
Yes, it began five today, six, six days ago.

00:01:04.839 --> 00:01:09.000
Yes, I think there are principal things you
can.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:15.200
Do it, and that is a very important moment
if you'll do this and if those side is ready,

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.330
it means that they are ready for the peace.

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:23.390
Speaker 1: The the level of I've never been
like a big Zelensky fan or anything like it,

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:32.670
but the level of poise that he is exhibiting
from a bunker separated from his family as

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:37.540
bombs are dropping, shelling is happening
all over the country.

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:39.340
It is just incredible.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:46.990
Speaker 3: If they don't, really, it means
that you are just, you know, just wasting

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:48.170
time.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:55.930
Do you think you're wasting your time or do
you think they're ready?

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:57.720
We'll see.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:08.229
Speaker 1: Just I mean, it is it is unbelievable
what is taking place right now and the question

00:02:08.229 --> 00:02:12.939
around the so-called negotiations is an important
question.

00:02:12.939 --> 00:02:19.099
We sort of just very casually talked about,
well, what is it Russia would want in such

00:02:19.099 --> 00:02:20.099
negotiations?

00:02:20.099 --> 00:02:25.700
I imagine Russia would want to officially
kind of see Ukraine give up on Crimea and

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:28.840
probably give up on the Donetsk and Luhansk
regions.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:29.840
That's that.

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:31.650
That's probably something Russia would want.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:34.120
Is that something Ukraine would be willing
to give?

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.890
It's hard to imagine.

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:43.359
On the other hand, I would imagine that Ukraine
would want Russia to accept that if Ukraine

00:02:43.359 --> 00:02:49.519
joins Naito or if Ukraine joins the EU, it
would not be opposed by Russia or seen as

00:02:49.519 --> 00:02:53.719
a sign of aggression or as a justification
for aggression by Russia.

00:02:53.719 --> 00:02:58.049
And it's very hard to imagine that that's
something that Russia would accept as well.

00:02:58.049 --> 00:03:00.949
So they talk about negotiations.

00:03:00.949 --> 00:03:06.889
It's in a practical sense, very difficult
to imagine what sort of agreement there could

00:03:06.889 --> 00:03:09.639
be that would be satisfactory to both sides.

00:03:09.639 --> 00:03:15.290
But that's why there is such a thing as professional
diplomacy and professional negotiators.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:17.730
We will continue seeing that there's sort
of the two tracks.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:23.450
There's the we are looking at doing some negotiation
on the border with Belarus, and there's at

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:26.480
some point Putin's going to make his play
for Kiev.

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:27.870
And that could be at any time.

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:33.180
And it's not obvious that Ukrainian forces
and volunteers are going to be able to repel

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:37.540
the Russian forces, so the next 24 48 hours
could be key.

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:38.889
We're going to take a quick break.

00:03:38.889 --> 00:03:44.309
The clips from that Zelensky interview, which
is very much worth watching, will be on our

00:03:44.309 --> 00:04:42.870
Instagram, which you can find at David Pakman
show.

